      "problem": "What is the value of $-3-(-1.5)$?",
      "worked_solution": "To subtract $-1.5$ from $-3,$ we combine the two negative signs to make a single plus sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-(-1.5)=-3+1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $-3+1.5,$ we start at  $-3$ and move $1$ place to the right. Then, we move another  $0.5$ places to the right: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14150464/assets/f8ebeccc7db234acc592ffd79aeeb92ce5ce5a756c4500019a1c5316f78d640d.png)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n-3-(-1.5)= -1.5.\n$$",
